Don't wait for your agent. Let it wait for you.

@thorstenball on why he never watches agents work: let them take as long as they need to comprehensively test changes in orbs, and focus on something else.

They don’t take up resources, or cost anything while they wait. We get back to them once we’re ready.

“I thought you guys were all about non-local dev, so why do you have the runners?”

@thorstenball on runners, which run Amp agents on machines you own: a Raspberry Pi at home, a lab of test hardware, GPU boxes, a macOS build machine.

“I think runners on different machines are non-local too, you know?”

You can now add live voice conversations, powered by @OpenAI's GPT-Live, to your Lovable apps.

@mgfeller built one where you can talk to Rocky from Project Hail Mary.

Amaze amaze amaze. https://t.co/IlL9JpkoYS
